<article class="env-definition" id="00WR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00WR">Definition <span data-tag="00WR">7.12.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site whose topology is subcanonical. The Yoneda embedding $h$ (see Categories, Section <a href="/tag/001L" data-tag="001L">4.3</a>) presents $\mathcal{C}$ as a full subcategory of the category of sheaves of $\mathcal{C}$. In this case we call sheaves of the form $h_ U$ with $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ <em>representable sheaves</em> on $\mathcal{C}$. Notation: Sometimes, the representable sheaf $h_ U$ associated to $U$ is denoted <em>$\underline{U}$</em>. </p>
</article>